/* book: lead: The square law assumes long channels, constant mobility and weak fields. Real transistors break all three. The vertical gate field drags carriers against the rough oxide interface, so mobility falls as the gate voltage rises: mobility degradation. The lateral drain field cannot speed carriers up beyond about 10⁷ cm/s: velocity saturation. And past pinch-off the channel gets shorter as VDS rises: c */
