/* book Worked example: Q: An nMOS has W = 1 µm, L = 0.25 µm, tox = 4 nm and an overlap Lov = 0.02 µm at each side (εox = 3.45 × 10⁻¹¹ F/m). Find Cox in fF/µm², CoxWL, Cov, and Cgs, Cgd and the total gate capacitance in saturation; then Cgs and Cgd in cutoff.
   1. Cox = 3.45 × 10⁻¹¹ / 4 × 10⁻⁹ = 8.625 × 10⁻³ F/m² = 8.625 fF/µm².
   2. CoxWL = 8.625 × 1 × 0.25 = 2.156 fF.
   3. Cov = 8.625 × 1 × 0.02 = 0.1725 fF per side.
   4. Saturation: Cgs = ⅔ × 2.156 + 0.1725 = 1.4375 + 0.1725 = 1.610 fF; Cgd = Cov = 0.1725 fF.
   5. Total gate capacitance = Cgs + Cgd = 1.610 + 0.1725 = 1.78 fF (Cgb = 0).
   6. Cutoff: Cgs = Cgd = 0.17 fF; the rest of the gate couples to the body, up to 2.16 fF.
   Answer: Cox = 8.63 fF/µm², CoxWL = 2.16 fF, Cov = 0.17 fF; in saturation Cgs = 1.61 fF, Cgd = 0.17 fF, total 1.78 fF; in cutoff Cgs = Cgd = 0.17 fF. */
